WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Architecture Overview: How DataGvat MCP Works

00:03.000 --> 00:30.000
Layered Architecture: Four layers working together

00:30.000 --> 01:00.000
Layer 1: MCP Protocol Layer handles communication with Claude Desktop

01:00.000 --> 01:30.000
Layer 2: FastMCP Framework provides tool registration and routing

01:30.000 --> 02:00.000
Layer 3: Enterprise Middleware includes retry logic, rate limiting, and structured logging

02:00.000 --> 02:30.000
Layer 4: Piveau Hub API Client interfaces with data.gv.at API

02:30.000 --> 03:30.000
Data Flow Step 1: User asks natural language query about Vienna transport datasets

03:30.000 --> 04:30.000
Data Flow Step 2: MCP tool invocation calls search_datasets with query parameters

04:30.000 --> 05:30.000
Data Flow Step 3: API request sent to Piveau Hub API with search parameters

05:30.000 --> 06:00.000
Data Flow Step 4: Structured response returns 12 datasets with metadata, quality scores, and download links
